<title>SINGAPORE: India sells Nov naphtha at NWE $27.47/T discount.</title>
<headline>India sells Nov naphtha at NWE $27.47/T discount.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) sold by tender 25,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) at $27.47 per tonne below Northwest European quotes on a free-on-board (fob) basis, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The cargo was sold to Swiss trader Glencore and is for November 14-16 lifting from Bombay on the Indian west coast.</p>
<p>The tender closed on October 31 and was valid until November 1.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3086)</p>
</text>
